{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And you shall call his name Ishmael</b> — The angel informed Hagar that his name would be Ishmael, in the manner of \"Behold, a son is born to the house of David, Josiah his name\" (I Kings 13:2). And he told her that she would call him thus and remember that Elohim heard her affliction. And Abraham on his own called his name thus — that El would hear and answer him — or a spirit of ruach ha-kodesh rested upon him according to Rashi's words, and he called him Ishmael because Elohim heard the affliction of his mother, as the angel had said. And what seems correct in my eyes is that the angel commanded Hagar to call him thus, but she was afraid, because she was a concubine, to give a name to the son of her master, so she disclosed the matter to him, and Abram fulfilled the word of HaShem; but Scripture had no need to elaborate on this."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:30:02.117060525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}